<div class="colophon">
    <section class="colophon__budgets" aria-labelledby="colophon-budgets">
        <h2 id="colophon-budgets">Budgets, enforced</h2>

        <p>
            A quality-focused Lighthouse CI run gates every pull request against fixed budgets, not
            targets. If a build exceeds one, the build fails. That is the same discipline described in the
            case studies, applied to this site's own delivery.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>{% metric "a11y_budgets" %}</li>
            <li>{% metric "perf_budgets" %}</li>
            <li>{% metric "weight_budgets" %}</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            Per the Web Almanac's 2025 crawl, most of the web fails the contrast and focus-visibility
            checks this site's accessibility budget requires on every route, in both themes, at both a
            desktop and a mobile viewport.
        </p>
    </section>

    <div class="colophon__aside">
        <section class="colophon__stack" aria-labelledby="colophon-stack">
            <h2 id="colophon-stack">Stack</h2>

            <p>
                Eleventy, Lightning CSS and Playwright are all build-time only: none of them ship a byte to the
                browser. Vanilla JavaScript with no client-side framework. Every font is self-hosted; every
                request on the published site resolves to this site's own origin.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="colophon__imagery" aria-labelledby="colophon-imagery">
            <h2 id="colophon-imagery">No AI-generated or stock imagery</h2>

            <p>
                Every photograph on this site is a real photograph of the person it depicts. There is no
                stock photography, no illustration set, and no AI-generated imagery anywhere on the site. The
                diagrams and charts are hand-authored SVG, drawn from this site's own published data.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
